---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SpecCard from '../components/SpecCard.astro';
import { isHeld } from '../data/publish-queue.js';

const held = isHeld('/perplexitybot/');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="PerplexityBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It | PromptDNS"
  description="PerplexityBot explained: what Perplexity's crawler does, its user-agent token, robots.txt behavior, how to verify it, and how to block or allow it."
  breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["AI Web Infrastructure", "/ai-web-infrastructure/"], ["PerplexityBot"]]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">PerplexityBot</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">PerplexityBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">PerplexityBot is Perplexity's crawler that builds the search index behind its answer engine. It honors robots.txt, and Disallow: PerplexityBot keeps your pages out of Perplexity answers. Genuine PerplexityBot fetches resolve to Perplexity-hosted addresses, which is how you verify them.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">PerplexityBot quick reference</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Operator</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Perplexity</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Purpose</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Search index and answers</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Opt-out</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Disallow: PerplexityBot</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Verification</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Reverse DNS to *.perplexity.ai</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Crawler specification" data-vs="speccard-wrap">
      <SpecCard
        name="PerplexityBot"
        operator="Perplexity"
        token="PerplexityBot"
        purpose="search index and answer engine"
        robots="honors Disallow: PerplexityBot"
        verify="Reverse DNS resolves to *.perplexity.ai"
        evidence="Documented"
        verified="2026-10-28"
        href="/ai-crawlers-list/"
      />
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>How to block PerplexityBot</h2>
      <p>Add this rule to your robots.txt at the root of your domain:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: PerplexityBot
Disallow: /</pre>
      <p>Blocking PerplexityBot removes your pages from Perplexity answers. Perplexity-User handles real-time user-initiated fetches under its own token.</p>

      <h2>How to allow PerplexityBot</h2>
      <p>If you want PerplexityBot to crawl your site, make sure no rule disallows it. An explicit allow looks like this:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: PerplexityBot
Allow: /</pre>
      <p>Then confirm from the live fetch with the <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI crawler checker</a>, which reads your published robots.txt the way a crawler would.</p>

      <h2>How to verify PerplexityBot</h2>
      <p>The reliable check is reverse DNS on the fetching IP address. Run the lookup below against any visitor claiming the PerplexityBot token; a genuine fetch resolves inside Perplexity's address space, and a spoofed one does not.</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">dig +short -x <fetching-ip>
# A genuine PerplexityBot fetch resolves to an Perplexity address</pre>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">Perplexity is the answer engine where blocking has the most immediate visible effect: opt out today and your pages stop appearing in answers within days, because its index is small and rebuilds often. That cuts both ways, so decide deliberately rather than by copying a template robots.txt.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I remove my site from Perplexity?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Add User-agent: PerplexityBot with Disallow: / to robots.txt. Perplexity documents that the crawler honors it.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is Perplexity-User?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">A separate Perplexity token for real-time fetches a user triggers. It has its own robots.txt rule, so you can allow answers from your pages on request without allowing crawling.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify PerplexityBot?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Reverse DNS on the fetching IP should resolve to a Perplexity address. Anything else claiming the token is spoofed.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Related:
        <a href="/ai-crawlers-list/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">all AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-block-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to block AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-allow-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to allow AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/robots-txt-guide/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">robots.txt guide</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
